From 5d03da29c8ed7e9e3cea30c92841aa9fbc6d8f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:14:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deps): peer-depend on the merged @strutvane/framework
 (one kernel)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

contracts, core, devkit and cli now ship inside @strutvane/framework
(framework CONSOLIDATION.md). This package still depended on the
published @strutvane/core and @strutvane/contracts, so installing it
next to the framework gave the app two kernels: container tokens are
Symbol()s and errors are checked with instanceof, so across the copies
LoggerToken did not match and a NotFoundError rendered as a 500
(verified in a test app: tokens differ, toProblem(...).status = 500).

- imports use @strutvane/framework/{core,contracts} (codemod of real
  specifiers only; comments untouched)
- @strutvane/framework is a peer (^0.1.0-next.1, which excludes the
  pre-merge 0.1.0-next.0 that has no ./core or ./contracts subpath) and
  a devDependency; the absorbed packages are gone
- tsdown never bundles the framework (/^@strutvane\/framework(\/|$)/)
- engines.node >=24.3 (blueprint §5)
- test/packaging.test.ts guards all of the above

Apply after @strutvane/framework 0.1.0-next.1 is published, then
regenerate the lockfile (npm install; dry run §6 step 8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
